= ZHANG, Qi -- Research
[https://feg.um.edu.mo/cee/ Department of Civil and Environmental Engineering], [https://www.um.edu.mo/ University of Macau]

== Research overview
My interests connect continuum mechanics, numerical discretization,
and learning methods for geomaterials.

=== Computational Poromechanics
I study the mechanical processes involved in the formation and recovery of
earth resources in sedimentary rocks, with an interest in energy and
environmental sustainability. Coupled fluid flow and solid deformation
are central to this work.

=== Smoothed Finite Element Method
My numerical-method interests include the smoothed finite element method.

=== Finite Element Method / Finite Volume Method
I am interested in finite element and finite volume discretizations for
complex geomaterials and nonlinear continuum mechanics, including their
connection to machine learning.

=== Neural Network
I am interested in physics-informed neural networks for geomaterials and
FEM/FVM discretization-guided machine learning. Related interests include
statistical learning for identifying hazards in mining and tunneling.

